---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const description =
  'Capture idea tickets, plan and implement through the ticket machine, and mirror external trackers with an explicit sync.';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Ticketing"
  description={description}
  current="/docs/ticketing"
  prev={{ href: '/docs/healer', label: 'Healer' }}
  next={{ href: '/docs/visualizer', label: 'Visualizer' }}
>
  <p>
    Tickets are the first-class unit of work. Configure ticket providers in
    <code class="hl">.adws/config/ticketing.yaml</code>, capture ideas with
    <span class="cmd">sssf ticket new</span>, and use the flows to plan and implement them.
    The board and command line share the same ticket machine.
  </p>

  <h2>Commands</h2>
  <pre><code>sssf ticket new "Explore dark mode"       # create an idea in needs-triage
sssf flow plan &lt;ticket-id&gt;                # write a spec and implementation tickets
sssf flow implement &lt;ticket-id&gt;           # implement one ready-for-agent ticket
sssf flow implement afk                    # work the ready queue
sssf ticket backlog &lt;ticket-id&gt; --feedback "Add regression coverage"
sssf ticket list [--backlog]
sssf ticket context &lt;ticket-id&gt; [--set "focus on OAuth"]</code></pre>
  <p>
    There is no direct ticket-run command. Flows are the only work-entry point; a plan flow
    creates implementation tickets, and implement claims only <code class="hl">ready-for-agent</code>
    tickets. Requeueing preserves run history.
  </p>

  <h2>Explicit tracker sync</h2>
  <pre><code>sssf ticket sync
sssf ticket sync --provider github</code></pre>
  <p>
    Sync pulls tickets from configured providers. Newly discovered tickets are untracked and
    start in <code class="hl">needs-triage</code>; they do not appear in the backlog until
    explicitly marked <code class="hl">ready-for-agent</code>. Sync then mirrors the ticket's
    machine control label, closes completed tickets, and appends completion or rejection
    comments, preserving unrelated labels. This is the only tracker writer; nothing pushes
    changes automatically.
  </p>
  <p>
    Provider configuration is per project. Jira uses its configured JQL; GitHub and GitLab use
    their provider configuration and origin repository. The internal provider needs no external
    credentials. Ticket records, runs, and history live in the project database at
    <code class="hl">.adws/data/sssf.db</code>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
